PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B2}
The decisive shape is the black C1-C2 stones. They are connected and their liberties are only B1 and B2; A2, B3-B4 are already being squeezed by the white stones on the right side. 

Playing B2 first removes one of those two liberties and puts the C1-C2 group in immediate atari. Black must reply B1 otherwise the group is captured on the next move. After 1.B2 2...B1 the black stones C1-C2-B1 have only A1 left, and the rest of the black formation is now forced to hang off the same liberty set because B2 also ties A2 to B3-B4. The follow-up 2...B1 3.A1 finishes the net and the whole black position is then captured with no useful counter-liberty available. B2 is therefore the initiating move of a forced kill sequence.

